Subject: [PATCH] Synchronize send quota tests instead of sleeping

TestQuotaBasics assumes goroutines will be scheduled within a few
milliseconds, while TestQuotaLoad starts 20000 parallel goroutines. The
20ms context can expire before a queued waiter is released on busy
builders, and sleeps do not establish FIFO acquisition order.

Run the basic test in a synctest bubble and wait for each waiter to block
before releasing quota. Check every acquisition result after release,
retaining the blocked-waiter, FIFO and quota-state assertions without
depending on host scheduling latency. TestQuotaContext continues to
exercise context cancellation, and TestQuotaLoad remains unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Reference: https://github.com/eclipse-paho/paho.golang/blob/v0.23.0/paho/session/state/sendquota_test.go

